# doc/codex/issues/0072 criterion 1, the 'ngspice -b -n < deck' row.  The deck
# is that issue's six-byte reproducer verbatim -- a title line and an .op dot
# card, no comment block, because the deck IS the reproducer; the commentary
# lives here, in the .invoke sibling and in Makefile.am.
#
# Before the fix at src/frontend/dotcards.c:225 this run died on
# assert(plot_cur->pl_dvecs != NULL) in ft_cktcoms() and the shell reported
# rc=134, 128+SIGABRT.  The criterion is that all three routes into that one
# call terminate normally, non-zero, with a diagnostic -- hence 1, and hence
# the .err sibling, which holds the same three lines as op-empty-netlist.err
# because the diagnostic is byte-identical on every route (measured).
#
# The driver's signal check is independent of this number and fires on any
# rc >= 128, so a regression back to the abort fails twice and names SIGABRT.
# That is the property this deck exists for; the status alone would not
# distinguish an abort from a deliberate exit(134).
1
